  "result": "Fixed: `IntRange` with `clamp=True` and an open bound now clamps to the nearest value inside the range instead of one step outside it.\n\nThe bug was in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. It returned `bound - dir`, which moved the wrong way. With `min_open=True` and a minimum of 0, `-5` clamped to `-1`, which is outside the range. I changed it to `bound + dir`, so that case now gives `1`, and `max=5, max_open=True` with input `9` gives `4`.\n\nI added both of those cases to the existing clamp parametrization in `tests/test_types.py`. I ran only that file, and it passes with 43 passed and 2 skipped. I did not run the full suite.",
